  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Toothpicks of equal length are used to build a rectangular grid as shown. If the grid is \\(20\\) toothpicks high and \\(10\\) toothpicks wide, then the number of toothpicks used is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(30\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(200\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(410\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(420\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(430\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "430"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1989-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "There are \\(11\\) vertical grid lines with \\(20\\) toothpicks each, and \\(21\\) horizontal grid lines with \\(10\\) toothpicks each. The total is \\[ 11\\cdot20+21\\cdot10=430. \\]\n\nThus the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Count horizontal and vertical toothpicks separately",
        "A grid \\(10\\) toothpicks wide has \\(11\\) vertical grid lines"
      ],
